  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice should now work. The tests (24 passed) and ruff both pass. I didn't add a test that reproduces the original failure.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function takes an invoice id and looks payments up by invoice. Passing the customer id meant it never found any payments. `refunded` stayed 0, and the \"no successful payment to refund\" error was raised even though the charge had succeeded.\n\n**Fix:** it now passes `invoice_id` instead.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}\n```",
